cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this experiment, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Trading Bot: an experiment with two Claude Opus 4.6s building and validating an algorithmic trading strategy"
abstract: >-
  A Discord trading-signal bot and Python backtesting and validation suite
  built almost entirely by two Claude Opus 4.6 instances. It includes
  walk-forward optimization, a stationary bootstrap on stitched out-of-sample
  returns, deflated and probabilistic Sharpe ratios, bar-permutation tests and
  Benjamini-Hochberg correction. Neither the mean-reversion strategy (SPY, QQQ,
  IWM) nor the 55-day Donchian trend-following strategy (23 ETFs) beat buy and
  hold. The project was archived on March 26, 2026.
